---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "run(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Create, list and remove git worktrees for very large repositories

Usage: wtm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new     Create a worktree and print its path
  ls      List the worktrees of this repository
  cd      Print the path of a worktree
  rm      Remove a worktree
  init    Rerun the init hook in a worktree
  gc      Empty the trash and prune stale git metadata
  doctor  Report on this repository, the data root and the creation method
  config  Print the effective configuration and where each value came from
  shell   Print a shell function that changes directory after `new` and `cd`
  agent   Output for coding agents

Options:
      --repo <PATH>  Operate on the repository at this path instead of the current directory
      --dir <PATH>   Data root holding the worktrees
  -q, --quiet        Silence progress messages
  -h, --help         Print help
  -V, --version      Print version
